{"/api/discogs/artist/10166203/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"10166203","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:10166203","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Snarexxx"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/10166203-Snarexx","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1067369/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1067369","image":"https://i.discogs.com/f_5ajVDYKmDWMRRNfMpJMbnujGN2WroATkZAsfjXOss/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:448/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNjcz/NjktMTcwODk1MjU2/MC05MzE3LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/QcCNB2igA16iPV47FM89GSo0CZ8NokRfAGaU4wzlrCg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNjcz/NjktMTcwODk1MjU2/MC05MzE3LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"French techno artist and DJ, born 24 June 1985 in Lyon, France. \nGesaffelstein is the main recording alias of Mike Lévy. \n\nHe has worked alongside and remixed tracks for such artists as varied as Tiga, Miss Kittin, ASAP Rocky, Lana Del Rey and Phoenix. He's also produced two tracks on album \"[m=567491]\", the sixth album of US rapper [a=Kanye West], including the lead single \"Black Skinhead\" and \"Send It Up\", both tracks produced with West, [a=Daft Punk], [a=Brodinski], and [a=Mike Dean]. \nGesaffelstein released his debut album \"[m=613908]\", in progress since 2011, on 28 October 2013 under [l=Parlophone] Records and [l=EMI Music]. \nHis remix of \"Shockwave\" by [a=The Hacker] is featured in the 2013 video game \"Grand Theft Auto V\", on the Soulwax FM radio station. \nIn 2010, he formed the Post-punk/Cold wave/New-wave Parisian band [a=FLYING TURNS (2)] with his childhood friend [a=Rudy Gueniche], which he departed one year later (switching from band member to producer) to focus on his solo carrier.\nGesaffelstein is a portmanteau of [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gesamtkunstwerk]Gesamtkunstwerk[/url] (\"total artwork\" in German, also the title of an album by the American electronic music act [a=Dopplereffekt]) and Albert Einstein. \n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1067369","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1325506,"name":"Mike Levy (3)"}],"groups":[{"active":false,"id":12456235,"name":"FLYING TURNS (2)"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Gessafelstein"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1067369-Gesaffelstein","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.gesaffelstein.com","http://gesaffelstein.bandcamp.com","http://www.bandsintown.com/a/511925-gesaffelstein","http://equipboard.com/pros/gesaffelstein","http://www.facebook.com/100044413990053","http://www.instagram.com/gesaffelsteinchannel","http://jaxsta.com/profile/93fa39d7-f4ed-4707-975c-a525a94e1485","http://www.last.fm/music/Gesaffelstein","http://musicbrainz.org/artist/cc3e537d-ff34-423f-8cd6-635a80f4dba7","http://myspace.com/gesaffelstein","http://www.songkick.com/artists/1893369-gesaffelstein","http://soundcloud.com/gesaffelstein","http://www.tiktok.com/@gesaffelstein","http://gesaffelstein-blog.tumblr.com","http://twitter.com/gesaffelstein","http://vimeo.com/gesaffelstein","http://www.whosampled.com/Gesaffelstein","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gesaffelstein","http://www.youtube.com/channel/UCneAnaIzzbA9MtT1jP4UkpA","https://web.archive.org/web/20091007233346/http://www.myspace.com/gesaffelstein1"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/291026/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"291026","image":"https://i.discogs.com/cX2agpHJTRtuJJHKF0YxtA2YDr_oBnZFpJsdEgwHyhM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:452/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5MTAy/Ni0xNjk2MzMzNzcy/LTg3MTIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/9dBOgRQ_7tFZM3o51AwZaHNTHAsEWSi4NjL2ioqlJHs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5MTAy/Ni0xNjk2MzMzNzcy/LTg3MTIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Musician and producer based in London.\r\nDele’s career began when he joined [a=Fela Kuti]'s [a=Egypt 80], where he played keyboards for seven years (1979-1986).\r\nDuring Fela’s incarceration in 1984, [a=Femi Kuti] - Fela’s son and Dele’s childhood school friend - took over the reins temporarily and led Egypt 80. During this period, Dele developed his arranging skills as the musical director of the band. He re-orchestrated and re-arranged for Egypt 80 and also handled the recruiting and training of new musicians.\r\nIn 1986 Dele and Femi left Egypt 80 to form their own band called [a=Femi Kuti & The Positive Force] of which Dele was the musical director and bandleader, responsible for recruiting and training the new band members. He was also the rhythm keyboard player and keyboard soloist.\r\nDele left Femi Kuti & The Positive Force in December 1995 and moved to London where he set about forming a new group, and the resulting projects reflect London’s multicultural environment, with a strong influence of jazz and shades of deep funk and Latin music, but all underpinned by the heavy grooves of Afrobeat’s Yoruba rhythm with Dele’s vocals very strongly in the Afrobeat tradition.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:291026","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":5332,"name":"Gbedu Resurrection"},{"active":true,"id":273534,"name":"Egypt 80"},{"active":true,"id":2886697,"name":"Lokkhi Terra"},{"active":true,"id":4696565,"name":"Dele Sosimi Afrobeat Orchestra"},{"active":true,"id":8212383,"name":"Femi Kuti & The Positive Force"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["D Sosimi","D. Sosimi","Dele","Dele Shosimi","Dele Soshimi","Dele Sosinmin","Dele Sousimi"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/291026-Dele-Sosimi","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.delesosimi.org","https://twitter.com/delesosimi","https://www.facebook.com/delesosimi/","https://www.instagram.com/delesosimi/","http://www.youtube.com/channel/UCgYSskfR-4k4bTqko1RAwZw","http://delesosimi.bandcamp.com","https://linktr.ee/delesosimi"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3196499/profile":{"cache